# Next.js + React + TypeScript

- Use App Router conventions (Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when needed).
- Prefer named exports for components/utilities unless the file already uses default export.
- Keep components pure; push side effects into hooks or event handlers.
- Use path aliases (`@/components`, `@/lib`, `@/hooks`) instead of deep relative imports.

## Accessibility + UI

- Ensure interactive elements have labels/aria where needed.
- Keep keyboard navigation intact (Radix components already help; don’t break it with div-onClick).

## Data / SEO files

- SEO endpoints live in `src/app/{sitemap.ts,robots.ts,manifest.ts}`; keep them deterministic and build-safe.
